"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>11<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Speed of sound<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>a<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>m/s<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>12<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Dryness fraction<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>x<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>kg/kg<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>13<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Specific Helmholtz free energy, f = u - Ts</td>\r\n"
"     <td>f<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>J/kg<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>14<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Specific Gibbs free energy, g = h - Ts</td>\r\n"
"     <td>g<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>J/kg<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>15<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Isenthalpic exponent, theta = -(v/p) (dp/dv)<sub>h</sub></td>\r\n"
"     <td>theta (&theta;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>1<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>16<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Isobaric volume expansion coefficient, alpha = v<sup>-1</sup> (dv/dT)<sub>p</sub></td>\r\n"
"     <td>alpha (&alpha;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"       <td>1/K<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>17<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Isochoric pressure coefficient, beta = p<sup>-1</sup>(dp/dT)<sub>v</sub></td>\r\n"
"     <td>beta (&beta;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>1/K<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>18<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>Isothermal compressibility, gamma = -v<sup>-1</sup>(dv/dp)<sub>T</sub></td>\r\n"
"     <td>gamma (&gamma;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>1/Pa<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <!-- <tr><td>f</td><td>Fugacity</td></tr> --> <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>19<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Dynamic viscosity</td>\r\n"
"     <td>eta (&eta;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>Pa s<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>20<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Kinematic viscosity</td>\r\n"
"     <td>nu (&nu;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>m<sup>2</sup>/s<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <!-- <tr><td>Pr</td><td>Prandtl number</td></tr> --> <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>21<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Thermal conductivity</td>\r\n"
"     <td>lambda (&lambda;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>W/(m K)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"     <tr>\r\n"
"     <td>22<br>\r\n"
"      </td>\r\n"
"      <td>Surface tension</td>\r\n"
"     <td>sigma (&sigma;)<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     <td>N/m<br>\r\n"
"     </td>\r\n"
"     </tr>\r\n"
"  </tbody>\r\n"
"</table>\r\n"
"        <p>The properties 1-11 are calculated by default with the functions for dynamic\r\n"
"        simulation, 2 of these variables are the dynamic states and are the inputs\r\n"
"        to calculate all other properties. In addition to these properties\r\n"
"        of general interest, the entries to the thermodynamic Jacobian matrix which render\r\n"
"        the mass- and energy balances explicit in the input variables to the property calculation are also calculated.\r\n"
"        For an explanatory example using pressure and specific enthalpy as states, see the Examples sub-package.</p>\r\n"
"        <p>The high-level calls to steam properties are grouped into records comprising both the properties of general interest\r\n"
"        and the entries to the thermodynamic Jacobian. If additional properties are\r\n"
"        needed the low level functions in BaseIF97 provide more choice.</p>\r\n"
"        <hr size=\"3\" width=\"90%\">\r\n"
"        <h4>Additional functions</h4>\r\n"
"        <ul>\r\n"
"        <li>Function <strong>boundaryvals_p</strong> computes the temperature and the specific enthalpy and\r\n"
"        entropy on both phase boundaries as a function of p</li>\r\n"
"        <li>Function <strong>boundaryderivs_p</strong> is the Modelica derivative function of <strong>boundaryvals_p</strong></li>\r\n"
"        <li>Function <strong>extraDerivs_ph</strong> computes all entries to Bridgmans tables for all\r\n"
"        one-phase regions of IF97 using inputs (p,h). All 336 directional derivatives of the\r\n"
"        thermodynamic surface can be computed as a ratio of two entries in the return data, see package Common\r\n"
"        for details.</li>\r\n"
"        <li>Function <strong>extraDerivs_pT</strong> computes all entries to Bridgmans tables for all\r\n"
"        one-phase regions of IF97 using inputs (p,T).</li>\r\n"
"        </ul>\r\n"
"        </html>"
msgstr "<html><h4>版本信息和修订历史</h4><li>\r\n"
"首次实施： <em>2000年7月</em> 由Hubertus Tummescheit与Jonas Eborn和Falko Jens Wagner共同为ThermoFluid Library开发</li>\r\n"
"<li>\r\n"
"代码重组、增强文档、添加额外功能： <em>2002年12月</em> 由<a href=\"mailto:Hubertus.Tummescheit@modelon.se\" target=\"\">Hubertus Tummescheit</a>&nbsp;完成，并转移到Modelica properties库。</li>\r\n"
"<li>\r\n"
"作者：Hubertus Tummescheit,<br><br>Modelon AB<br><br>Ideon Science Park<br><br>SE-22370 Lund, Sweden<br><br>电子邮件：hubertus@modelon.se<br></li>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"1997年9月，国际水蒸汽物性协会（<a href=\"http://www.iapws.org\" target=\"\">IAPWS</a>&nbsp;）采用了一种新的水和蒸汽热物性的表述，用于工业用途。这个新的工业标准称为“国际水蒸汽物性协会工业用水和蒸汽热物性表述”（IAPWS-IF97）。 IAPWS-IF97的表述取代了之前的工业标准IFC-67。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"基于这个新的表述，W. Wagner和A. Kruse于1998年4月在Springer-Verlag出版了一本名为“<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-03529-0\" target=\"\">Properties of Water and Steam</a>&nbsp;”的新蒸汽表。这个蒸汽表，参考文献<a href=\"#steamprop\" target=\"\">[1]</a>&nbsp;是双语的（英语/德语），包含了对IAPWS-IF97方程的完整描述。这个参考文献是此实现的权威信息来源。 已经由国际水蒸汽物性协会（<a href=\"http://www.iapws.org\" target=\"\">IAPWS</a>&nbsp;）发布了一个几乎相同版本的蒸汽表，并允许在注明 <a href=\"http://www.iapws.org\" target=\"\">IAPWS</a>&nbsp; 的情况下重新发布相关信息。 此文档与本库一起分发，作为<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/IF97.pdf\" target=\"\">IF97.pdf</a>&nbsp;。 另外，由<a href=\"http://www.iapws.org\" target=\"\">IAPWS</a>&nbsp;发布的动力黏度（标准文档：<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/visc.pdf\" target=\"\">visc.pdf</a>&nbsp;）和导热系数（标准文档：<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/thcond.pdf\" target=\"\">thcond.pdf</a>&nbsp;）的输运性质方程以及表面张力方程（标准文档：<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/surf.pdf\" target=\"\">surf.pdf</a>&nbsp;） 也包含在此库中，以供参考。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"BaseIF97.mo中的函数是低级函数，应仅在标准用户级函数Water.mo中不包含所需属性时使用。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"基于IAPWS-IF97，Modelica函数可用于计算最常见的热物性（热力学和传输性质）。实现需要Modelica.Thermal.Properties库中Common.mo文件中的部分公介质属性基础设施。与IF97.pdf文档中记录的IF97版本相比，为了提高动态模拟的性能，进行了一些扩展。用于计算属性的输入变量仅对有限数量的变量对实现，这些变量对作为动态状态是有意义的：（p，h），（p，T），（p，s）和（d，T）。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<hr/><p>\r\n"
"<br>\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"<br>\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<h4><a href=\"\" target=\"\">1. IAPWS-IF97的结构和区域</a>&nbsp;</h4><p>\r\n"
"国际水蒸汽物性协会1997年工业表述包括一组方程，涵盖以下有效性范围：\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<table style=\"width: auto;\"><tbody><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">273.15 K &lt; <em>T</em> &lt; 1073.15 K</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><em>p</em> &lt; 100 MPa</td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1073.15 K &lt; <em>T</em> &lt; 2273.15 K</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><em>p</em> &lt; 10 MPa</td></tr></tbody></table><p>\r\n"
"图1显示了整个IAPWS-IF97有效性范围分为的5个区域。区域的边界可以直接从图1中获取，除了区域2和3之间的边界；这个边界，大致对应于等熵线<sup><em>s = 5.047 kJ kg-1K-1</em></sup>，由相应的辅助方程定义。区域1和2都分别由特定吉布斯自由能的基本方程<em>g( p,T )</em>覆盖，区域3由特定赫姆霍兹自由能的基本方程<em>f ( r,T)</em>覆盖，而对应于区域4的饱和曲线由饱和压力方程<sub><em>ps( T )</em></sub>覆盖。高温区域5也由<em>g( p,T )</em>方程覆盖。这些方程，在图1中以矩形框显示，构成<em>基本方程</em>。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<table style=\"width: auto;\"><tbody><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"image.png\" data-href=\"\" style=\"\"/></td></tr></tbody></table><p>\r\n"
"除了这些基本方程外，还为区域1、2和4提供了<em>逆向方程</em>，形式为 <em>T( p,h )</em>和<em>T( &nbsp;p,s )</em>用于区域1和2，以及<sub><em>Ts( p )</em></sub>用于区域4。这些逆向方程在图1中以灰色标记，它们的开发方式使其在数值上与相应的基本方程非常一致。因此，在计算区域 1 和区域 2 的 p,h 和 p,s 以及区域 4 的 p 的函数时，无需进行任何迭代。由于新工业标准 IAPWS-IF97 的开发采用了这一特殊概念，最重要的属性可以极其快速地计算出来。所有Modelica函数都针对短计算时间进行了优化。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"新工业表述IAPWS-IF97的各个方程的完整描述在<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/IF97.pdf\" target=\"\">IF97.pdf</a>&nbsp;中给出。关于IAPWS-IF97的全面信息（要求、概念、准确性、沿区域边界的一致性、与IFC-67相比的计算速度提高等）可从<a href=\"modelica://Modelica/Resources/Documentation/Media/Water/IF97documentation/IF97.pdf\" target=\"\">IF97.pdf</a>&nbsp;或[2]中获取。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"<a href=\"\" target=\"\">[1]<em>Wagner, W., Kruse, A.</em> Properties of Water and Steam / Zustandsgrößen von Wasser und Wasserdampf / IAPWS-IF97. Springer-Verlag, Berlin, 1998.</a>&nbsp;\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"[2] <em>Wagner, W., Cooper, J. R., Dittmann, A., Kijima, J., Kretzschmar, H.-J., Kruse, A., Mareš R., Oguchi, K., Sato, H., Stöcker, I., Šifner, O., Takaishi, Y., Tanishita, I., Trübenbach, J., and Willkommen, Th.</em> The IAPWS Industrial Formulation 1997 for the Thermodynamic Properties of Water and Steam. ASME Journal of Engineering for Gas Turbines and Power 122 (2000), 150 - 182.\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<hr/><p>\r\n"
"<br>\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"<br>\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<h4>2. 可计算属性 &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</h4><table style=\"width: auto;\"><tbody><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><strong>通用名称</strong><br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><strong>缩写</strong><br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"><strong>单位</strong><br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 1<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Pressure</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">p<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Pa<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 2<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Temperature</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">T<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">K<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 3<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Density</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">d<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">kg/m<sup>3</sup><br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 4<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific volume</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">v<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">m<sup>3</sup>/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 5<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific enthalpy</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">h<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 6<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific entropy</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">s<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/(kg K)<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 7<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific internal energy<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">u<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 8<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific isobaric heat capacity</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">c<sub>p</sub><br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/(kg K)<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\"> 9<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific isochoric heat capacity</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">c<sub>v</sub><br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/(kg K)<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">10<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Isentropic exponent, kappa = -(v/p) (dp/dv)<sub>s</sub></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">kappa (κ)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">11<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Speed of sound<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">a<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">m/s<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">12<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Dryness fraction<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">x<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">kg/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">13<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific Helmholtz free energy, f = u - Ts</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">f<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">14<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Specific Gibbs free energy, g = h - Ts</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">g<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">J/kg<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">15<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Isenthalpic exponent, theta = -(v/p) (dp/dv)<sub>h</sub></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">theta (θ)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">16<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Isobaric volume expansion coefficient, alpha = v<sup>-1</sup> (dv/dT)<sub>p</sub></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">alpha (α)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1/K<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">17<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Isochoric pressure coefficient, beta = p<sup>-1</sup>(dp/dT)<sub>v</sub></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">beta (β)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1/K<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">18<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Isothermal compressibility, gamma = -v<sup>-1</sup>(dv/dp)<sub>T</sub></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">gamma (γ)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">1/Pa<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">19<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Dynamic viscosity</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">eta (η)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Pa s<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">20<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Kinematic viscosity</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">nu (ν)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">m<sup>2</sup>/s<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">21<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Thermal conductivity</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">lambda (λ)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">W/(m K)<br></td></tr><tr><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">22<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">Surface tension</td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">sigma (σ)<br></td><td colSpan=\"1\" rowSpan=\"1\" width=\"auto\">N/m<br></td></tr></tbody></table><p>\r\n"
"默认情况下，属性1-11通过动态模拟函数计算，其中2个变量是动态状态，并且是计算所有其他属性的输入变量。除了这些普遍关心的属性外，还计算了热力学雅各布矩阵的条目，这些条目在属性计算的输入 变量中明确了质量和能量平衡。有关使用压力和比焓作为状态的解释性示例，请参阅示例子库。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<p>\r\n"
"对蒸汽属性的高级调用被分组成记录，其中包括一般属性和热力学雅可比的条目。如果需要额外的属性，BaseIF97中的低级函数提供了更多选择。\r\n"
"</p>\r\n"
"<hr/><h4></h4><h4></h4><h4>附加函数</h4><li>\r\n"
"函数<strong>boundaryvals_p</strong>根据p计算两个相界面上的温度、比焓和熵</li>\r\n"
"<li>\r\n"
"函数<strong>boundaryderivs_p</strong>是<strong>boundaryvals_p</strong>的Modelica导数函数</li>\r\n"
"<li>\r\n"
"函数<strong>extraDerivs_ph</strong>使用输入(p,h)计算IF97的所有单相区域的Bridgman表的所有条目。热力学曲面的所有336个方向导数都可以作为返回数据中两个条目的比值来计算，详细信息请参见Common库。</li>\r\n"
"<li>\r\n"
"函数<strong>extraDerivs_pT</strong>使用输入(p,T)计算IF97的所有单相区域的Bridgman表的所有条目。</li>\r\n"
"</html>"

